# lens-test-shape.allow — scenarios that call a Go identifier in code yet are integration-level.
#
# Format: <path><TAB><heading substring>. Every entry needs a reason above it: this file is
# where the judgment is recorded, not where it is hidden. Reasons come from the 2026-09-06
# audit (per-scenario verdicts, tightened rubric: a fixture directory is the component's
# input; KEEP needs two or more components on the path, a spex subcommand, a module
# boundary, or an external system the process does not own).

# The spec-derived file set and the journal-sourced event bracket are asserted together, so 
# resolver and store both act on the path.
spec/map/test_context_resolver.md	S1: Resolve context for a live component by identity hash

# The assertion is that the bracket follows the journal lineage's latest event, which only the 
# resolver plus the store's fold can produce.
spec/map/test_context_resolver.md	S1b: Bracket follows the lineage's latest event

# Bracket widening across consecutive task_retargeted receipts is asserted through the resolver 
# over the store's fold.
spec/map/test_context_resolver.md	S1d: Retargeted task widens the bracket

# The null bracket is asserted against a journal that has history but no task-bearing event, so 
# the store's fold is load-bearing alongside the spec derivation.
spec/map/test_context_resolver.md	S1c: Live node with no task-bearing event serves a null bracket

# The task id must be mapped to an identity hash through the journal fold before the spec 
# derivation runs, so two components chain.
spec/map/test_context_resolver.md	S2: Resolve by task id reaches the same node

# The removed node's whole answer (biography plus bracket) comes from the store's fold surfaced 
# through the resolver.
spec/map/test_context_resolver.md	S5: Removed node resolves from the journal

# The not-found error must distinguish unknown-everywhere from removed-but-remembered, which 
# requires the spec scan and the journal fold to both come up empty.
spec/map/test_context_resolver.md	E2: Key known to neither spec nor journal

# Explicit end-to-end pairing where real trees flow through Diff into Classify and the composed 
# result is asserted.
spec/merkle/test_diff_classification.md	S14: Diff then Classify end-to-end integration

# Asserts the composition of the two components by checking every built hash against HashFile 
# and HashChildren bottom-up.
spec/merkle/test_hashing.md	S6: BuildTree hashes propagate bottom-up

# Multi-module build whose root hash is asserted against HashChildren, exercising both 
# components together.
spec/merkle/test_hashing.md	S8: Multi-module tree construction

# Epic emission, parent refs and epic label come from Resolver plus Labeler acting together 
# inside Build().
spec/plan/test_changeset_builder.md	Proposal epic parents every non-epic create

# Layer ordering, layer edges and profile-driven refusals are asserted on the emitted op stream 
# produced by several components.
spec/plan/test_changeset_builder.md	Layer edges follow the profile's order

# Resolver's unresolvable-dep error is asserted as it surfaces out of Builder.Build().
spec/plan/test_changeset_builder.md	Unresolvable dep is a plan error

# Explicit cross-component scenario joining Resolver classification, sorter ordering and 
# builder composition or refusal.
spec/plan/test_changeset_builder.md	Cross-component scenario: dep classification round-trip through Builder

# Cycle is detected by the sorter and asserted as the error propagated out of Builder.Build().
spec/plan/test_changeset_builder.md	Cross-component scenario: cycle detection surfaces through Builder.Build error

# spec_node_kind fill and profile-driven layering are asserted together on built changesets 
# under two profiles.
spec/plan/test_changeset_builder.md	Cross-component scenario: spec_node_kind and layer per declared type come from the profile



# Asserts the copied file and the journal line appended through the map module's MappingStore, 
# crossing the module boundary.
spec/proposal/test_registration.md	S1: Register a valid project proposal

# Asserts the refusal leaves no journal line in the map module's journal as well as no file.
spec/proposal/test_registration.md	S3: Reject project proposal with missing sections

# A profile.json fixture is resolved by the schema module's ProfileLoader and drives which 
# arrays SpecReader walks, so the scenario crosses a module boundary.
spec/render/test_spec_reading.md	S9: Declared arrays are read through the resolved profile

# The scenario drives the build harness itself, rebuilding the binary and comparing hashes 
# across builds.
spec/schema/test_schema_loading.md	E3: Schema content is deterministic across builds


# The assertion is on profile-composed schemas resolved outside the checker, crossing into the 
# schema/profile module.
spec/validator/test_conformance_and_content.md	S16: Conformance runs against the profile-composed schemas

# The walked type set comes from the resolved profile, so profile resolution outside the 
# component is on the asserted path.
spec/validator/test_conformance_and_content.md	S18: Content resolution walks the declared content-bearing types
